+## Append-only batch bce3f075-provider-01: exact direct-command/OpenAPI consumers
+
+Batch files live under `batches/bce3f075-provider-01/`, based on checkpoint 5
+`bce3f075156a86be345821499c04628cb35c2762`. Fifty schema rows have explicit
+field/ref/anyOf/container interpretations, exact real source readers and complete
+A/B/negative task configurations, 50 narrow C0 definitions and 200 future real
+productive-boundary cases. Current totals: 1,222 rows, 4,058 case bodies (1,075
+narrow source/definition passed, 2,983 future not-run); **none accepted**.
+
+### Actual owning schema API is not productive runner enforcement
+
+The exported registry provider-schema validator rejects unknown keys in actual
+schema controls. `provider-validator-callers.log` shows its declaration/export
+only; resolver calls are in the separate exported plan resolver API. Productive
+runner preparation carries `node.configuration` unchanged, validates generic
+invocation shape, and uses the verified isolated package snapshot/provider child
+execution. That child initializes/execututes the provider; it does not call the
+owning configuration schema validator. Actual tested provider execution ignores
+an unknown config key that the owning schema rejects. This supersedes prior
+unspecific claims that remote runner/provider execution enforces the owning schema.
+It does not remove F-VAL unknown-key obligations: proposed owner/ref/schema
+validation must occur before real command/network effects, without a second author.
+
+`check.mjs` deliberately uses **instrumented capability capture transport** for
+provider controls. Actual provider configuration/schema logic, request forwarding,
+OpenAPI task assertions and direct-command filesystem copies execute; the capture
+returns fictional response data. This is not actual command execution, external
+HTTP dispatch, Core admission, isolated runner/grant enforcement, report finalizer
+acceptance, or original F-EFFECT credit. Future case fixtures explicitly require
+those actual real boundaries and same-boundary positive controls.
+
+A separate genuine `NetworkHttpCapabilityInvoker` probe uses an actual ephemeral
+localhost server. It proves the current source class's caps, not full-role/grant
+acceptance: timeout/response cap zero reject before request; same 1,500-byte body
+rejects at 1,024 and succeeds at 2,048. Current OpenAPI provider forwards requested
+zero values, although the owning schema rejects them; the actual HTTP runtime
+rejects them separately. Provider timeout is `min(requested ?? 10000, invocation
+.timeoutMs)`; response bytes default 1,048,576 without provider artifact-byte clamp.
+Actual retained HTTP caps remain another authority and cannot be fabricated.
+
+Direct command arguments/environment/cwd and evidence declarations remain task
+authority, not a new global CONFIG writer. Fixed JUnit/LCOV codec identities have
+no fictional independent valid B. OpenAPI scalar anyOf nodes are alternative forms
+of the same task value, not three settings. Endpoint name is used only with the
+deployment fixture and dormant with URL/public endpoint. Tags add non-explicit
+operations; cleanup ordering is best effort after transport failure and does not
+prove durable effect reconciliation. No recovery/idempotency claim follows from
+these current guards or from captured transport responses.
+
+### Per-candidate manual dispositions and exact remaining guard obligations
+
+`candidate-dispositions.json` contains 64 source-line-reviewed records, exact
+original text/digests and existing setting links. Remaining original candidates:
+4,578 unreviewed. Ten reviewed records explicitly remain open numeric safety/
